          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रुकिए (rukie) — \"please wait\", \"please stop\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रुक (ruk, the stem of the verb \"to stop\") + -ie, the respectful ending of बोलिए becomes रुकिए (rukie). रुकिए (rukie), एक मिनट (ek minaṭ) — \"wait, one minute\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रुकिए (rukie) is the verb ruknā, \"to stop\", with the respectful ending -ie. CDIAL lists ruknā under a reconstructed rokk, \"stop\", whose link with Sanskrit rudh-, \"to obstruct\", it calls not clear (CDIAL 10827)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Wait, one minute, again, louder."
